## 6. Data model (core tables)

```
devices(id, serial, transport, resolution_w, resolution_h, status, last_heartbeat)
app_instances(id, device_id, package, clone_id)
accounts(id, app_instance_id, game_uid, nickname, server, role, alliance_id, enabled)
tasks(id, name, config_json, enabled_for_roles[])
task_runs(id, account_id, task_name, started_at, ended_at, status, result_json, error, screenshot_ids[])
screenshots(id, account_id, captured_at, screen_id, object_key, sha256)
alliances(id, tag, name, server)
members(id, alliance_id, game_uid, name, rank, joined_at, left_at, active)
member_aliases(id, member_id, alias, source, created_at)
participation_facts(...)                    -- see above
member_participation_weekly(member_id, period_key, metric, value, computed_at)
train_schedule(id, alliance_id, date, conductor_id, backup_id, honored)
review_queue(id, screenshot_id, raw_text, candidates_json, status, resolved_by)
audit_log(id, actor, action, entity, before, after, at)
```

---

## 7. Interfaces

**REST** (`/api/v1`): fleet CRUD, `POST /accounts/{id}/tasks/{name}/run`, `POST /fleet/pause`, `GET /members`, `GET /rankings?period=`, `GET /participation/{member_id}`, `POST /review/{id}/resolve`, `GET /messages/weekly`.

**WebSocket** `/ws/fleet`: live task status, per-device thumbnails (throttled to ~1 fps), error stream.

**MCP server** — build this; it's how you'll actually operate the thing day to day from Claude:

```
fleet_status()                          → devices, accounts, running tasks
run_task(account, task, args)           → dispatch, returns run_id
pause_fleet(reason) / resume_fleet()
capture_now(account, route)             → force an analytics capture
alliance_rankings(period, metric)       → leaderboard rows
member_report(name_or_uid)              → full participation profile
inactivity_watchlist(days)              → kick candidates
review_pending()                        → OCR items needing confirmation
draft_alliance_message(template, period)
```

**Dashboard** (server-rendered + htmx, or SvelteKit — avoid a heavy SPA): Fleet, Tasks, Members, Rankings, VS Compliance, Train, Review Queue, Settings. Mobile-first for the review queue specifically, since you'll clear it from your phone.

